"published_at":"2019-12-13T08:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":0,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Dota 2 with large scale deep reinforcement learning","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/dota-2-with-large-scale-deep-reinforcement-learning"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"3b009c78076ab800ed9096f7a2e58bfe89d9c8fea202aed80091f0a040e2068d","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/deep-double-descent","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"19b78ea11083222742b3","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/deep-double-descent","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2019-12-05T08:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":0,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"We show that the double descent phenomenon occurs in CNNs, ResNets, and transformers: performance first improves, then gets worse, and then improves again with increasing model size, data size, or training time. This effect is often avoided through careful regularization. While this behavior appears to be fairly universal, we don’t yet fully understand why it happens, and view further study of this phenomenon as an important research direction.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Deep double descent","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/deep-double-descent"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"5361bb4f3514638bb7aeefef91ec524b5c62140bd5eca87c390b4edcc4e2568e","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/procgen-benchmark","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"2f2d250f7b2e219f5b56","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/procgen-benchmark","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2019-12-03T08:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":0,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"We’re releasing Procgen Benchmark, 16 simple-to-use procedurally-generated environments which provide a direct measure of how quickly a reinforcement learning agent learns generalizable skills.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Procgen Benchmark","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/procgen-benchmark"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"c64345bf2493639eaa7f331a33883c46068450f96dbaf03ae6f6f68e23fb2aa4","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/safety-gym","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"c23fd24e1cf8ad7361de","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/safety-gym","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2019-11-21T08:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":0,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"We’re releasing Safety Gym, a suite of environments and tools for measuring progress towards reinforcement learning agents that respect safety constraints while training.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Safety Gym","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/safety-gym"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"0c6642d2ff36f543def73384972fa75f232afb639e70c7c8c24d78f5cd3601f7","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/benchmarking-safe-exploration-in-deep-reinforcement-learning","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"20e4089b4976e60b1889","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/benchmarking-safe-exploration-in-deep-reinforcement-learning","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2019-11-21T08:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":0,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Benchmarking safe exploration in deep reinforcement learning","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/benchmarking-safe-exploration-in-deep-reinforcement-learning"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"9b4fffbc79cbd4b9d368338d18ac74d31c1187d03bc1def73a4cb7fcf07d55c8","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/gpt-2-1-5b-release","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"31066a8ed5c3a077637d","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/gpt-2-1-5b-release","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2019-11-05T08:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":0,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"As the final model release of GPT-2’s staged release, we’re releasing the largest version (1.5B parameters) of GPT-2 along with code and model weights to facilitate detection of outputs of GPT-2 models. While there have been larger language models released since August, we’ve continued with our original staged release plan in order to provide the community with a test case of a full staged release process. We hope that this test case will be useful to developers of future powerful models, and we’re actively continuing the conversation with the AI community on responsible publication.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"GPT-2: 1.5B release","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/gpt-2-1-5b-release"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"d6abc61e39bb0adc8312dea838294ca80f7b3cdcab460c901668a1bcc5c3e17e","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/solving-rubiks-cube","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"69dcd4141a73ff97c0fd","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/solving-rubiks-cube","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2019-10-15T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":0,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"We’ve trained a pair of neural networks to solve the Rubik’s Cube with a human-like robot hand. The neural networks are trained entirely in simulation, using the same reinforcement learning code as OpenAI Five paired with a new technique called Automatic Domain Randomization (ADR). The system can handle situations it never saw during training, such as being prodded by a stuffed giraffe. This shows that reinforcement learning isn’t just a tool for virtual tasks, but can solve physical-world problems requiring unprecedented dexterity.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Solving Rubik’s Cube with a robot hand","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/solving-rubiks-cube"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"e6c7b82ec6f9d4cd125257151d972709e4dfba0bc19375edaa9eebd851a3d1cf","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/openai-scholars-2020","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"0dc505378e653ae31d9a","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/openai-scholars-2020","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2019-10-11T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":0,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"We are now accepting applications for our third class of OpenAI Scholars.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"OpenAI Scholars 2020: Applications open","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/openai-scholars-2020"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"1a36632618a74d91b9a7a701165bacbe035a0893d84dc85b6872e9415bc53856","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/fine-tuning-gpt-2","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"dd954fe97ea9426708a1","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/fine-tuning-gpt-2","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2019-09-19T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":0,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"We’ve fine-tuned the 774M parameter GPT-2 language model using human feedback for various tasks, successfully matching the preferences of the external human labelers, though those preferences did not always match our own. Specifically, for summarization tasks the labelers preferred sentences copied wholesale from the input (we’d only asked them to ensure accuracy), so our models learned to copy. Summarization required 60k human labels; simpler tasks which continue text in various styles required only 5k. Our motivation is to move safety techniques closer to the general task of “machines talking to humans,” which we believe is key to extracting information about human values.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Fine-tuning GPT-2 from human preferences","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/fine-tuning-gpt-2"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"5b431b57c97085ece7c3810b61942e4de44149b3a2dffb26d6d3d26c5e45228e","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/emergent-tool-use","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"bb4559fb85eefb33bf8c","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/emergent-tool-use","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2019-09-17T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":0,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"We’ve observed agents discovering progressively more complex tool use while playing a simple game of hide-and-seek. Through training in our new simulated hide-and-seek environment, agents build a series of six distinct strategies and counterstrategies, some of which we did not know our environment supported. The self-supervised emergent complexity in this simple environment further suggests that multi-agent co-adaptation may one day produce extremely complex and intelligent behavior.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Emergent tool use from multi-agent interaction","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/emergent-tool-use"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"35c1517fba045169b900689ab4c66aa3c9c6e5e1c1c898b0bc57aeeffe431fb5","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/testing-robustness","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"90184b0d09ceaa8b2866","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/testing-robustness","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2019-08-22T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":0,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"We’ve developed a method to assess whether a neural network classifier can reliably defend against adversarial attacks not seen during training. Our method yields a new metric, UAR (Unforeseen Attack Robustness), which evaluates the robustness of a single model against an unanticipated attack, and highlights the need to measure performance across a more diverse range of unforeseen attacks.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Testing robustness against unforeseen adversaries","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/testing-robustness"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"82f8a9e49dcf95caf742058284146db9ffb0ed56a1a10a501efb55d39a5da07e","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/gpt-2-6-month-follow-up","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"aec2fcecd95ebb499e08","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/gpt-2-6-month-follow-up","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2019-08-20T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":0,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"We’re releasing the 774 million parameter GPT-2 language model after the release of our small 124M model in February, staged release of our medium 355M model in May, and subsequent research with partners and the AI community into the model’s potential for misuse and societal benefit. We’re also releasing an open-source legal agreement to make it easier for organizations to initiate model-sharing partnerships with each other, and are publishing a technical report about our experience in coordinating with the wider AI research community on publication norms.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"GPT-2: 6-month follow-up","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/gpt-2-6-month-follow-up"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"dbbdfffa7c5b13d192c0c81fe75f13beedcbb92cf7f7e311db904266fa694384","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/learning-day","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"8ace9587a2b910d793ca","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/learning-day","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2019-08-01T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":0,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"At OpenAI, each Thursday is Learning Day: a day where employees have the option to self-study technical skills that will make them better at their job but which aren’t being learned from daily work.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Learning Day","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/learning-day"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"d0f45599aa4fc2c121c195fd307e099edacce75c1ec3edad80e73a18fb8a4092","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/microsoft-invests-in-and-partners-with-openai","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"7835b0b036cfe198fc49","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/microsoft-invests-in-and-partners-with-openai","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2019-07-22T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":0,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"Microsoft is investing $1 billion in OpenAI to support us building artificial general intelligence (AGI) with widely distributed economic benefits. We’re partnering to develop a hardware and software platform within Microsoft Azure which will scale to AGI. We’ll jointly develop new Azure AI supercomputing technologies, and Microsoft will become our exclusive cloud provider—so we’ll be working hard together to further extend Microsoft Azure’s capabilities in large-scale AI systems.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Microsoft invests in and partners with OpenAI to support us building beneficial AGI","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/microsoft-invests-in-and-partners-with-openai"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"5b34eb9aa64cf515157068a276085ad63763b14ab15bf040f230eb67e398ce68","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/cooperation-on-safety","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"c411875eb53ea2c9fda5","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/cooperation-on-safety","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2019-07-10T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":0,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"We’ve written a policy research paper identifying four strategies that can be used today to improve the likelihood of long-term industry cooperation on safety norms in AI: communicating risks and benefits, technical collaboration, increased transparency, and incentivizing standards. Our analysis shows that industry cooperation on safety will be instrumental in ensuring that AI systems are safe and beneficial, but competitive pressures could lead to a collective action problem, potentially causing AI companies to under-invest in safety. We hope these strategies will encourage greater cooperation on the safe development of AI and lead to better global outcomes of AI.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"Why responsible AI development needs cooperation on safety","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/cooperation-on-safety"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"146fc8a1ca6deba15d6e18709cde8fbe3b2a35f6c9d9f6d6d78c3d33faaa8abf","date_precision":"instant","discovered_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","doi":null,"external_id":"https://openai.com/index/symposium-2019","first_seen":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","id":"ab8dbdfbc1279f5594d1","links":[],"provenance":[{"article_url":"https://openai.com/index/symposium-2019","found_at":"2026-10-16T19:26:59Z","name":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","url":"https://openai.com/"}],"published_at":"2019-06-05T07:00:00Z","relevance":"candidate","relevance_reason":"discovery candidate; needs review","revision_count":0,"score":0,"source":"OpenAI","source_id":"openai","source_url":"https://openai.com/","summary":"We hosted the first OpenAI Robotics Symposium on April 27, 2019.","summary_kind":"publisher excerpt","title":"OpenAI Robotics Symposium 2019","topics":[],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://openai.com/index/symposium-2019"},{"aliases":[],"arxiv_id":null,"authors":[],"content_hash":"efabbd94707bb129caa8903852771d0f66e1c920cd9be8b9a1772f331b4d8258","date_precision":"insta